1f:["$","p",null,{"style":{"color":"var(--text-secondary)","marginBottom":"1.5rem","lineHeight":1.7},"children":"React client hosts the Monaco Editor connected via WebSocket to a Node.js signaling cluster. Text mutations are structured as Yjs CRDT operations, eliminating central conflict resolution bottlenecks. Redis Pub/Sub synchronizes messages across multiple Node.js socket server instances. A decoupled sandbox worker executes user-submitted code in disposable, resource-constrained Docker containers."}]
29:T5ac,+-----------------------+             +-----------------------+
|    BROWSER CLIENT A   |             |    BROWSER CLIENT B   |
|  (Monaco Editor + Yjs)|             |  (Monaco Editor + Yjs)|
+-----------------------+             +-----------------------+
            \                                     /
             \ (WebSocket WSS)                   / (WebSocket WSS)
              v                                 v
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|                   NODE.JS / TYPESCRIPT GATEWAY              |
|         (Socket.io Room Hub + Authentication Handshake)     |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
                               |
                               v
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|                     REDIS PUB/SUB & STATE                   |
|     - Room State Presence & Cursor Position Broadcasting    |
|     - Active Collaboration Session Registry                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
                               |
                               v
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|                 SANDBOXED CODE EXECUTION RUNNER             |
|   - Isolated Docker Containers (CPU/RAM/Network Throttled)  |
|   - Subprocess Execution with 5-Second Timeout Deadlines    |
